                "content": "### Detailed Solution ###\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\nS_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z^{2}\\mid a\\ge 1,\\;b\\ge 1,\\;a+b\\le n+1\\},\n\\qquad |S_n|=\\frac{n(n+1)}2 .\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\n\nA line is called **sunny** iff it is **not** parallel to any of the three lines  \n\n\\[\ny=0,\\qquad x=0,\\qquad x+y=0 .\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 1.  A bound for a sunny line  \n\nLet \\(L\\) be a sunny line.  Write its reduced slope as  \n\n\\[\nm=\\frac pq\\qquad(q>0,\\;(p,q)=1),\n\\]\n\nwith the additional condition \\((p,q)\\neq(1,-1),(-1,1)\\) (otherwise \\(L\\) would be parallel to \\(x+y=0\\)).  \nIf \\((x_1,y_1),(x_2,y_2)\\in L\\cap\\mathbb Z^{2}\\) then  \n\n\\[\ny_2-y_1=m(x_2-x_1)=\\frac pq\\,(x_2-x_1),\n\\]\n\nhence \\(p\\mid (y_2-y_1)\\) and \\(q\\mid (x_2-x_1)\\).  Consequently all lattice points of \\(L\\) are of the form  \n\n\\[\n(x_0,y_0)+t\\,(q,p),\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb Z .\n\\tag{3}\n\\]\n\nInside the triangle \\(S_n\\) we have  \n\n\\[\n1\\le x\\le n,\\qquad 1\\le y\\le n,\\qquad x+y\\le n+1 .\n\\]\n\nFrom (3) we obtain  \n\n\\[\n|t|\\le\\frac{n+1}{|p|+|q|}\\, .\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(L\\) is not parallel to any of the three forbidden directions, at least one of \\(|p|,|q|\\) is non‑zero and \\(|p|+|q|\\ge 2\\) (the only case with \\(|p|+|q|=1\\) would be a horizontal, vertical or slope \\(-1\\) line, all of which are non‑sunny).  \nHence (4) gives  \n\n\\[\n|t|\\le\\Big\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Big\\rfloor .\n\\]\n\nIncluding the point corresponding to \\(t=0\\) we obtain the **sunny‑line bound**\n\n\\[\n|L\\cap S_n|\\le\\Big\\lfloor\\frac{n+1}{2}\\Big\\rfloor .\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 2.  Columns of \\(S_n\\)\n\nFor a fixed abscissa \\(a\\;(1\\le a\\le n)\\) define the *\\(a\\)-th column*\n\n\\[\nC_a=\\{(a,b)\\in S_n\\}.\n\\]\n\nFrom the definition of \\(S_n\\),\n\n\\[\n|C_a|=h_a=n+1-a .\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nThus the